# Launcher edge (LOCAL mode): the host-facing door to the brain API for local-mode users, whose Hermes
# runs on their own PC (docs/LOCAL_MODE_DESIGN.md). Same default-deny proxy and format as
# launcher-edge.allowlist (route_proxy.py; METHOD /path or METHOD /prefix*; query ignored).
#
# NOT here, on purpose:
#   POST /launcher/launch     hosted only: a desktop token for a per-user backend local mode does not have
#   POST /launcher/byok/link  hosted only: local mode has no server-side model key
#   POST /launcher/introspect never on any edge (see launcher-edge.allowlist)
# Every route below also answers 404 to a hosted tenant (routes.py _require_local), and a brain token is
# honoured only for a local-mode, non-cancelled tenant (tokens.resolve_brain).
GET  /launcher/healthz          # uptime check: {"ok": true}, no auth, no data
POST /launcher/auth/invite      # redeem a single-use invite -> device session
POST /launcher/auth/refresh     # rotate the refresh token (reuse revokes the device)
POST /launcher/auth/revoke      # sign out: revoke this device
GET  /launcher/devices          # account: this user's signed-in devices
POST /launcher/devices/*        # account: /{id}/revoke (own devices only; 404 otherwise)
GET  /launcher/me               # user, tenant, brain names
GET  /launcher/compat           # Hermes desktop versions we accept
GET  /launcher/local/policy     # the Hermes setup to apply (no secrets)
POST /launcher/local/posture    # the launcher's reading of that setup (a Hermes Cloud agent signs out)
POST /launcher/local/launch     # brain token, only after a good report
GET  /launcher/local/memory     # the user's own memories (int3 app, launcher token)
POST /launcher/local/memory/*   # save|recall|forget (Hermes plugin, brain token); delete (int3 app)
